  "id": "Compound::DB00482 - Gene::23632",
  "verbalization": "Celecoxib, a selective COX-2 inhibitor, is shown to bind to multiple calcium-binding proteins (Ca5a, Ca5b, and Ca6), which in turn participate in Carbonate Dehydratase Activity. This activity is ultimately linked to Ca14, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Celecoxib influences Ca14 through its interaction with calcium-binding proteins. The evidence indicates that Celecoxib may modulate Ca14 via a pathway involving calcium-dependent enzymatic activity, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The shared involvement of Carbonate Dehydratase Activity in the pathways suggests a common functional role, potentially linking Celecoxib to Ca14 through a calcium-dependent enzymatic mechanism. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of calcium-binding proteins in mediating the effects of Celecoxib on Ca14, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct relationship.",
